For a parallel plate capacitor $\mathrm{C}=\frac{\varepsilon_{0} \mathrm{ A}}{\mathrm{ d}} \begin{aligned}
\therefore \quad \mathrm{A}=\frac{\mathrm{Cd}}{\varepsilon_{0}}=\frac{1 \times 10^{-3}}{8.85 \times 10^{-12}}\\
&=1.13 \times10^{8} \mathrm{ m}^{2}
\end{aligned}$ This corresponds to area of square of side $10.6 \mathrm{ km}$ which shows that one farad is very large unit of capacitance.
